exports.description:
Normalize a Standard Schema issue path into the canonical dot-index string.
Segments may be bare `PropertyKey` or `{ key }` objects (vendor-dependent);
an empty/absent path → "" = the form-level bucket.

A registry holding every catalog validator and codec:
- `luhn` — card number checksum (empty passes; `required` is separate);
- `notExpired` — `"MM/YY"` or `{ month, year }` not in the past (valid through the month's end);
- `matrixRows` — args `{ rows, required: "all" | n }`: how many matrix rows must be answered;
- `timeRange` — args `{ min?, max? }` as `"HH:mm"`: inclusive bounds on a time of day;
- `richTextLength` — args `{ min?, max? }`: characters of a rich-text value's text content (JSON doc or HTML), not its markup;
- `availability` — a weekly availability value has well-formed, ordered, non-overlapping ranges per day;
- `color` — a canonical `#rrggbb` (anything `parseColor` accepts passes, so a draft typed as `rgb()` is not an error);
- `contrast` — args `{ against, min? }`: WCAG contrast of the colour with `against` is at least `min` (default 4.5, AA body text); meant as a `warn` rule;
- `latLng` — `{ lat, lng }` inside the WGS 84 bounds;
- `dateRules` — args `{ min?, max?, disablePast?, disableFuture?, rules?, today?, timeZone? }`: a date (or each end of a `{ from, to }` range) is not blocked by `@kitora/pickers/core`'s date rules; the message is the rule's reason, else the catalog's (see catalog/date-rules.ts);
- codecs `cardNumber` (grouped ⇄ digits) and `cardExpiry` (digits → `MM/YY`).

Fold one inspection into the render stats: a field whose record object was
replaced since `prev` re-rendered once (fields subscribe by record identity);
the reason is the members that differ. Untouched fields keep their stats.

What a RichTextField holds:
- `RichTextDoc` — format `json` (default), a ProseMirror JSON document;
- `string` — format `html`, the editor's HTML;
- `null` — an empty document (no text), so `required` treats it as empty.
